Note: DX-12 NoteValue-rate delay smoke test
Note: Phase 22 plan 22-04 -- exercise delay(Buffer, NoteValue, Double, Double) synced to MusicalContext.Tempo
Note: At 120 BPM, EIGHTH = 250ms; at 240 BPM, EIGHTH = 125ms
Note: Existing ms-rate overload (delay buf 250.0 0.5 0.4) must remain unchanged

use "@std"
use "@audio"
use "@notation"

Note: createSineTone(duration, frequency, amplitude) -- 0.5s @ 440Hz at amp 0.8 (44100 stereo)
Buffer src = (createSineTone 0.5 440.0 0.8)

Note: At 120 BPM, EIGHTH note delay = 250ms
tempo 120 {
    Buffer wet = (delay src EIGHTH 0.5 0.4)
    (writeWav "tests/output/dx_delay_eighth_120.wav" wet)
}

Note: At 240 BPM, EIGHTH note delay = 125ms (tempo doubles, time halves)
tempo 240 {
    Buffer wet2 = (delay src EIGHTH 0.5 0.4)
    (writeWav "tests/output/dx_delay_eighth_240.wav" wet2)
}

Note: Existing ms-rate overload still works (regression gate)
Buffer wet3 = (delay src 250.0 0.5 0.4)
(writeWav "tests/output/dx_delay_msrate.wav" wet3)

(print "DX-12 delay sync: PASSED")
